  <!-- ================================================================== -->
  <!-- 8. WHY OST IS NOT A SCAM — FULL TRANSPARENCY -->
  <!-- ================================================================== -->
  <section id="transparency" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why OST Is Not a Scam &mdash; Full Transparency</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        You've been lied to by too many projects. We understand.
        Here is everything about us, laid bare. Verify it all yourself.
      </p>

      <div class="manifesto">
        <p class="manifesto-lead">
          Trust is earned with facts, not promises.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>No pre-mine. No hidden allocations. No &ldquo;team tokens.&rdquo;</strong><br>
          The OST mint starts at zero. Every single token in existence was minted
          through the public, auditable <code>confidential_mint</code> instruction.
          There are no secret wallets, no locked vesting schedules benefiting insiders,
          and no tokens set aside for a "team" that disappears. The supply grows only
          through transparent, community-visible operations.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Open source from day one.</strong><br>
          Every line of Rust, every TypeScript function, every deploy script &mdash;
          it's all on GitHub. The Anchor program, the client SDK, this website &mdash;
          all public. Read the code yourself. If you find a flaw, open a PR. If you
          find something shady, tell the world. We have nothing to hide because there
          is nothing to hide.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Real company, real founder, real jurisdiction.</strong><br>
          OST is operated through a Panama S.A. (Sociedad An&oacute;nima), a legal
          entity chosen for its neutrality and crypto-friendly regulation. The founder
          is a builder from Mexico &mdash; not anonymous, not hiding behind a pseudonym.
          The Panama company documents are available for public inspection. We chose
          transparency over mystery because this project belongs to everyone, not to
          a shadowy founding team.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Why Panama? Why not &ldquo;no country&rdquo;?</strong><br>
          Because today, in 2026, a legal entity is still needed to sign contracts,
          hold domain names, and interact with the non-crypto world. Panama provides
          a neutral, internationally recognized framework. But OST the <em>token</em>
          is nationless by design. It doesn't belong to Panama, Mexico, or any flag.
          It belongs to the people who use it &mdash; all of them, everywhere.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>The space story is real.</strong><br>
          The 0.1% DAO fee isn't a marketing gimmick. It flows into a transparent,
          on-chain treasury governed by staked OST holders. The treasury's mandate
          is to fund decentralized physical infrastructure: satellite relays, mesh
          networks, orbital compute nodes. Every disbursement is voted on publicly
          and executed on-chain. You can verify every SOL, every vote, every proposal
          in the block explorer. The satellites aren't a metaphor. They're a budget line.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>What we believe:</strong><br>
          We are all brothers and sisters. Borders are lines on maps drawn by power;
          they don't exist in our hearts. OST is simply a tool that lets us trade
          freely and privately, the way humans were always meant to. This is not
          about rebellion. It's about remembering that we belong to each other.
        </p>

        <p class="manifesto-closing">
          Read the code. Check the company. Verify the treasury.<br>
          <strong>Then decide for yourself.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

